From 9353f3cf458afecd8d575286c9d1edbaea760b65 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: serlk <22211586+Serlk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 02:16:51 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] linker: add a vendor profile with BIONIC_VENDOR_ROOT
 library directories

Allow loading bionic-linked libraries out of a directory tree laid out
like the Android partitions. When BIONIC_VENDOR_ROOT is set, the linker
adds <root>/vendor/lib64, <root>/vendor/lib64/hw,
<root>/apex/<vndk>/lib64 (BIONIC_VNDK_APEX, default
com.android.vndk.v34) and <root>/system/lib64 to the fixed library
search directories, in that order, so that libraries from vendor/ see
the VNDK copies of the framework libraries before system/lib64.

Absolute Android paths (/vendor/lib64/hw/foo.so, /system/lib64/bar.so)
passed to dlopen or found in DT_NEEDED are resolved below the root
first. Absolute paths that point into one of the fixed library
directories are now also accepted as bionic-linked libraries, like
paths matching BIONIC_LD_LIBRARY_PATH already were.

libm.so is mapped to libc_bio.so.0 in this profile, since libm is part
of libc on musl and glibc and a foreign libm must never be loaded.
override_map_append() is exported from the config helper for this.

SOPATH_MAX grows to 16 to make room for the extra directories.
